{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T09:18:44.778Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7687d94a08e852f40579b9f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-todos-tnou"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Packed acceptance reports a bare timeout without scenario or subprocess diagnostics"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-todos#165 (filed 2026-10-28, missed by the blind issue watch). scripts/accept-packed.ts on current main still throws only '<command> exceeded <deadline>ms and was terminated' in its ETIMEDOUT branch (line ~80): it drops the captured stdout/stderr and the scenario name, so a hung 'bun init -y' (observed once on release PR #164's Node 26 job, 2026-10-28) cannot be diagnosed — no scenario, no output, no environment hint. The releases themselves have since succeeded (v2026.10.29 through v2026.10.31 green), so this is the remaining diagnostic gap, not a release blocker: include the scenario name and captured output in timeout errors and fail closed with the scenario list when a scenario never starts."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","diagnostics","gh:unbraind/pm-todos#165"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:18:44.778Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:18:44.778Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"688704e9796c759303a4ff04da2265cfc7091a9155c5a2d606c9f7e14c8b